From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iio: adc: mt6359-auxadc: report BAT_TEMP in millivolts

The Q25 port converted the BAT_TEMP NTC divider voltage with an invented
linear formula, 25 + (850 - mV) / 18 degC. It roughly matches the real NTC
curve near room temperature but reports ~72 degC at 0 V, so a lost NTC
bias produced false critical-temperature shutdowns. Return the divider
voltage in mV and convert it with the vendor 10k NTC table in DT
(generic-adc-thermal temperature-lookup-table).
---
--- a/drivers/iio/adc/mt6359-auxadc.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/mt6359-auxadc.c
@@ -834,10 +834,12 @@
 			*val = 25000 + ((750 - v_mv) * 1000) / 4;
 			break;
 		case PMIC_AUXADC_CHAN_BAT_TEMP:
-			v_mv = div_s64((s64)(*val) * desc->r_ratio.numerator * cinfo->vref_mV,
-				       (s64)desc->r_ratio.denominator << chan->scan_type.realbits);
-			*val = 25000 + ((850 - v_mv) * 1000) / 18;
-			break;
+			/*
+			 * BAT_TEMP is the battery NTC divider voltage, not a
+			 * temperature: report millivolts and let the consumer
+			 * (generic-adc-thermal lookup table) convert it.
+			 */
+			fallthrough;
 		default:
 			*val = div_s64((s64)(*val) * desc->r_ratio.numerator * cinfo->vref_mV,
 				       (s64)desc->r_ratio.denominator << chan->scan_type.realbits);
